{"id":"chatcmpl-5760492f-2be6-43db-9622-274014fd27b7","object":"chat.completion","created":1795248140,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task resolves a binary laterality question (left vs right basal atelectasis) on a chest X-ray where the primary challenge is spatial orientation, not pathology detection. The successful strategy queries multiple independent vision-language models with laterality-explicit prompts, then aggregates by majority/consistency rather than trusting any single tool. The key insight is that when tools disagree, the resolution comes from cross-validation across independent assessors and weighting those that give specific, side-explicit answers.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a task hinges on spatial laterality (left/right, above/below), explicitly instruct each tool to report patient-side orientation rather than assuming it, since models often default to image-side.\",\n    \"Query multiple independent assessors in parallel and resolve disagreement by consistency/majority across specific answers, discounting non-specific or failed responses.\",\n    \"Escalate to additional independent tools specifically when earlier outputs conflict, rather than accepting the first or most verbose answer.\",\n    \"Prefer tools that produce specific, falsifiable answers (named side + finding) over vague descriptions when aggregating evidence for a forced-choice decision.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging multiple-choice\": \"Frame prompts to force side/location specificity; run 2-4 independent VLMs; decide by agreement among specific answers, not by any single model.\",\n    \"Conflict resolution across tools\": \"When tools disagree, add a fresh independent assessor targeting the exact disputed dimension (here, laterality) instead of re-prompting the same tool.\",\n    \"Forced-choice under uncertainty\": \"Weight evidence by specificity and independence; treat non-specific or failed outputs as abstentions rather than votes.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm each tool's answer explicitly names the patient side (not image side) before counting it as evidence.\",\n    \"Verify the final choice is supported by at least two independent, specific tool outputs; if not, query one more independent assessor.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":619,"total_tokens":1034,"completion_tokens":415,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":619},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":415}}}